TEXT 144 208 Left 2 ;Sip switch simulation
TEXT 536 -200 Left 5 ;Capdyn input control
TEXT 1280 144 Left 2 ;EN1_CAP triggered high when backup cap first charges up to 5.5V\ntriggered low when backup cap discharges down to 3.85 V (clamping diodes limit)
TEXT 520 144 Left 2 ;Window type voltage monitor simulator:\nThis lower limit is dictated by clamping diodes at the switches
TEXT 2248 88 Left 2 ;INPUT power drive EN1:\nEN1_CAP signals that the backup capacitor is in its range, so capdyn can be safely charged.\nNOTRDY allows power to be redirected to the backup cap when the main bank is charged\nto the desired stage. EN2 allows capdyn to still accumulate energy when load is activated (EN2).
TEXT 1136 -216 Left 2 ;This part of the circuit controls input power flow to the main bank.\nInput is activated only if the backup can supply power to CapDyn.\nIf input is deactivated, power flows to the backup capacitor.
TEXT -1736 -128 Left 2 ;VDDR actually powers VDD of digital components\nWe don't power them directly from VDDRSIG because\nthe CD4000 power consumption values are off.
TEXT -864 -120 Left 2 ;Power supply for the models of the SIP switches.\nThe models don't source their power from V_BCK, \nthey source it from their input.
TEXT -2352 2456 Left 2 !.param PDN=1Meg
TEXT 1704 -328 Left 2 ;VT is low when the Vcpdn is under the threshold (load off)\nVT is driven high by the load when Vcpdn overcomes the threshold (load on)
TEXT 768 2456 Left 2 ;wake-up stage is re-initialized whenever VDD power is lost and bank is empty.
